PERSONAL FORK — NOT INTENDED FOR PUBLIC CONSUMPTION. This is a personal working copy of plashchynski/viewssld (https://github.com/plashchynski/viewssld), kept for experiments. It is unmaintained and unsupported, may diverge from upstream or be rewritten at any time, and nothing here is released for others to use. Use the upstream project instead.

viewssld is an open source SSL decryption daemon for Snort and other network Intrusion Detection System (IDS).

== Requirements
* libpcap
* libssl (openssl)
* libdssl you can download it here: https://github.com/downloads/plashchynski/viewssld/libdssl-2.1.1.tar.gz


== Download
You can download the latest viewssld version here: https://github.com/downloads/plashchynski/viewssld/viewssld-0.7.0.tar.bz2


== Installation and Usage
See http://resources.infosecinstitute.com/ssl-decryption/ for more details. Please note that libdssl is no longer available at the atomiclabs svn archive so the libdssl download link in the article doesn't work. You can download libdssl here: https://github.com/downloads/plashchynski/viewssld/libdssl-2.1.1.tar.gz


== Support
Need some help? Feel free to create an issue https://github.com/plashchynski/viewssld/issues
